/target
/dist
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store
/handoff.md
# A CANONICAL blend is canonical BY LOCATION: `assets/<id>/<id>.blend` — one directory under
# `assets/`, which is where the trio rule looks for a source and where every derived path is cut
# from. Those are tracked (LFS, `.gitattributes`), because the committed derivative — the glb, the
# LOD chain, the manifest — must travel with the source it was cut from or nothing can re-cut it;
# the shared material library at `assets/materials/materials.blend` is one of them, and every tank
# blend links its substances out of it. A second vehicle is tracked by that rule and edits nothing
# here. Everything else blend-shaped is local authoring scratch: a blend anywhere else, Blender's
# own `.blend1` rolling backup, and the hand-made `.bak` snapshots a session leaves beside it.
*.blend
!assets/*/*.blend
*.blend1
*.bak

# Scratch output of a hand-run texture bake. The BAKED glb is the tracked one; an asset ships one
# glb and this line makes a second one impossible to commit by accident.
*.mipped.glb

# Firecrawl research scratch (web search/scrape cache)
.firecrawl/

# Cloudflare wrangler local cache
.wrangler/
__pycache__/

# Renders the LOD chain's rendered-difference gate writes when it is pointed at a kept directory.
scripts/lod/out/
